Z||000010||MrPBody||12-10-2000||09:48 AM||||Once upon a time in a former life, I hatched the inspiration to use an emission control air pump to supercharge a B&S.  Never did it, though.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||JohnnyK||12-10-2000||04:11 PM||||Emission control air pump? Explain.||||reg||1
Z||000012||MrPBody||12-10-2000||06:42 PM||||This probably won't work . . .<P>Use a belt-driven air injection pump.  Mount the B&S carburetor on the pump intake; pipe pump output into B&S intake.<P>Lots of cars formerly used air injection.  I think catalytic converters made it obsolete.<BR>||||reg||1
